{"id": "EUVD-2026-86203", "enisaUuid": "c951cfa9-c196-31a0-bc34-aecb5b08af65", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: au1000: move free_irq out of the close-time spinlocked section\n\nau1000_close() calls free_irq() while aup->lock is still held with\nspin_lock_irqsave(). free_irq() can sleep because it takes the IRQ\ndescriptor request mutex, so it does not belong inside the close-time\nspinlocked section.\n\nThis was found by our static analysis tool and then confirmed by manual\nreview of the in-tree au1000_close() .ndo_stop path. The reviewed path\nkeeps aup->lock held across the MAC reset, queue stop and\nfree_irq(dev->irq, dev).\n\nA directed runtime validation kept that ndo_stop carrier and the same\nfree_irq(dev->irq, dev) operation under the driver lock. Lockdep reported\n\"BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context\" and \"Invalid wait\ncontext\" while free_irq() was taking desc->request_mutex, with\nau1000_close() and free_irq() on the stack.\n\nDrop aup->lock before freeing the IRQ. The protected close-time work still\nstops the device and queue before IRQ teardown, but the sleepable IRQ core\npath now runs outside the spinlocked section.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f86bca5b7857b85bfa8afdb4fa895d7c0a3f7ebc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26fd652915123a690f19d62b253b545a53f3cd51", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d514b08ed61fdffe23604fd3e9e53c07cbe5ac3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1b5a13249975fec3cf654efa84f57118db2da2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4536667fba8ddbaff2f2a135080ae6aabf737b5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc2233f1ab2a1ca562869bca6987d7477671388c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f48763beab4eea41fc480c9702ec6eebe8d75e4f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xvh7-3cp2-m6qq", "CVE-2026-93815"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ad36c95-bfef-3d51-8001-451e0e92ed8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <f86bca5b7857b85bfa8afdb4fa895d7c0a3f7ebc"}, {"id": "23a4cf01-e9a7-30ab-8f69-a1dc8f4bc9d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "25136950-30d7-3614-bfd3-fe5e1271a92c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <4536667fba8ddbaff2f2a135080ae6aabf737b5e"}, {"id": "4d05f6cb-54e1-3789-b946-07288589a886", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "541e228c-9737-3c1c-b58b-223033f3da85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "7ed4598d-3b4b-35e2-971c-98ec12ab07e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <d514b08ed61fdffe23604fd3e9e53c07cbe5ac3e"}, {"id": "7fcf1332-e9d6-342d-9a35-5d09999da559", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "a015c0d7-f86c-3803-a879-ca300bae1774", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <26fd652915123a690f19d62b253b545a53f3cd51"}, {"id": "a9ad6bd1-3893-3d25-ac47-ccf6ce498bb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <fc2233f1ab2a1ca562869bca6987d7477671388c"}, {"id": "c4e45b14-00e9-3b08-bb04-9f30ba1ae1cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <e1b5a13249975fec3cf654efa84f57118db2da2c"}, {"id": "c5e40f89-1b57-39ac-a329-4d02c1f0ff6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "c9ea0147-73e7-3683-be